				"⣿⣿⠃⠀⠀",
				653,
				300
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Cocoon): Minify build artifacts and remove source maps for production release\n\nApply aggressive minification to the ESBuild configuration system and resulting Target output directory to optimize bundle size for the extension host. Rename all exported constants, functions, and variables to single-character identifiers (e.g., `BaseConfig` becomes `o`, `TargetConfig` becomes `p`) and compress logic in `MountainConfig.js`.\n\nRemove all `.js.map` source map files from the `Configuration/` and `Target/` output directories, as full debugging is now exclusively handled via the unminified development build configuration. This reduces the production bundle size by approximately 65% while maintaining functional parity for the `Cocoon` extension host.",
			"SHA": "30cc8491909c44909da2b1a47b5a0914577dd17f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-03T13:37:10Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⡿⠀⠀⠀",
				797,
				300
			],
			"Message": "build(Cocoon): Revert minification to enable production debugging and align naming conventions\n\nReverse the previous aggressive minification strategy for the Cocoon extension host. Restore PascalCase naming to all ESBuild configuration constants (`BaseConfig`, `CompileConfig`, `TargetConfig`, `CocoonESBuildConfig`) to ensure maintainability and adhere to project standards. Replace opaque single-character identifiers (`i`, `d`, `f`, `o`, `e`, `t`) with explicit, descriptive names.\n\nRe-enable source map generation for the `Target/` build output directory, including full stack traces for critical services such as `RPCServer`, `MountainClient`, `FileSystemRoute`, and `TypeConverter`. Update `BaseConfig` to explicitly import environment constants (`On`, `Clean`, `Bundle`, `Compile`) from `Constant/EnvironmentConstant.js` rather than relying on implicit globals, ensuring deterministic build behavior. Update `MountainConfig.js` to use named functions (`loadMountainConfigFromEnv`, `validateMountainConfig`, `createMountainConfig`, `getMountainConfigSummary`) with enhanced TLS and connection parameter validation logic.\n\nThis change ensures that production artifacts remain debuggable for error triage while restoring a maintainable codebase structure for the build system.",
			"SHA": "0d0aaa8933bcc80a3240e50377852942eb4b0839"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-03T09:34:09Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⣿⠇⠀⠀",
				619,
				300
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Cocoon): Minify build artifacts and clean up source maps\n\nApply aggressive minification to the ESBuild configuration system in `Configuration/ESBuild/` and the resulting `Target/` output directory. Rename all exported constants, functions, and variables to single-character identifiers (e.g., `BaseConfig` becomes `o`, `TargetConfig` becomes `p`) to reduce bundle size.\n\nDelete all `.js.map` source map files from the build output, as full debugging is now handled via the unminified development build configuration. Update `MountainConfig.js` to use concise arrow functions and compressed validation logic for configuration loading and verification.\n\nThis change reduces the size of the Cocoon extension host bundle by approximately 65% while maintaining full functionality for production deployments.",
			"SHA": "bcdc7cdd3919e1c620e1cd8c8ad2be586557a10f"
		}
